IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je21-nouns`
IMPORT `je21-seat-2-powers-and-effects`

-- je21-tests-seat-2-powers-and-effects: tests for the exported questions about powers, repeal, amendment and annulment.
-- The expected values were written by hand from Articles 4 to 11 before the module was run.
-- The questions use the default reading of each fork, which je21-seat-defaults names; the other readings are tested in the rule modules' tests.

§ `Seat questions -- powers and effects -- tests`

§§ `Article 4`

#ASSERT `Does Article 4 cover this power?` `a power to make an appointment` TRUE
#ASSERT `Does Article 4 cover this power?` `a power to do any other thing for the purposes of the legislation` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Does Article 4 cover this power?` `a power of none of these kinds` TRUE BECAUSE "Article 4(1) covers a power given by Jersey legislation to do one of the things it lists, and the Law does not say whether Article 4 covers any other power"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Does Article 4 cover this power?` `a power to establish an entity` FALSE BECAUSE "Article 4(1) covers a power given by Jersey legislation to do one of the things it lists, and the Law does not say whether Article 4 covers any other power"
#ASSERT `May a power given by Jersey legislation be exercised before that legislation is in force?` `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a power given by Jersey legislation be exercised before that legislation is in force?` `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` TRUE FALSE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 4(2) permits a power given by Jersey legislation to be exercised after the legislation is made, whether or not it is in force, unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a power given by Jersey legislation be exercised before that legislation is in force?` `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` TRUE TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 4(2) permits a power given by Jersey legislation to be exercised after the legislation is made, whether or not it is in force, unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a power given by Jersey legislation be exercised before that legislation is in force?` `a power to make Jersey subordinate legislation` FALSE TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 4(2) permits a power given by Jersey legislation to be exercised after the legislation is made, whether or not it is in force, unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a power given by Jersey legislation be exercised before that legislation is in force?` `a power of none of these kinds` TRUE TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 4(2) permits a power given by Jersey legislation to be exercised after the legislation is made, whether or not it is in force, unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
#ASSERT `Is bringing the subordinate legislation into force on this day not barred by Article 4(3)?` (YMD 2022 6 1) (YMD 2022 6 1)
#ASSERT `Is bringing the subordinate legislation into force on this day not barred by Article 4(3)?` (YMD 2022 6 2) (YMD 2022 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Is bringing the subordinate legislation into force on this day not barred by Article 4(3)?` (YMD 2022 5 31) (YMD 2022 6 1)

§§ `Article 5`

#ASSERT `Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `an existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` FALSE
#ASSERT `Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `a penalty, forfeiture or punishment incurred for an offence committed, or a breach, before the repeal` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `an existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` TRUE BECAUSE "Article 5(2) leaves these things untouched when Article 5 applies and no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what a repeal does to them otherwise"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` FALSE TRUE `it was repealed` `an existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` FALSE BECAUSE "Article 5(2) leaves these things untouched when Article 5 applies and no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what a repeal does to them otherwise"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` TRUE FALSE `it was repealed` `an existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` FALSE BECAUSE "Article 5(2) leaves these things untouched when Article 5 applies and no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what a repeal does to them otherwise"
#ASSERT `Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` FALSE TRUE `it expired` `an existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` FALSE
#ASSERT `Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` FALSE TRUE `it otherwise ceased to have effect` `an existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Does a repeal leave this thing untouched?` FALSE TRUE `it has not ended` `an existing right, interest, title, immunity, privilege, obligation or liability acquired, accrued or incurred under it` FALSE BECAUSE "Article 5(2) leaves these things untouched when Article 5 applies and no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what a repeal does to them otherwise"
#ASSERT `May a proceeding or penalty about the repealed legislation still go ahead?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a proceeding or penalty about the repealed legislation still go ahead?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` FALSE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 5(3) lets a proceeding about, or a penalty for, something mentioned in paragraph (2) go ahead as if the legislation had not been repealed when Article 5 applies, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a proceeding or penalty about the repealed legislation still go ahead?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 5(3) lets a proceeding about, or a penalty for, something mentioned in paragraph (2) go ahead as if the legislation had not been repealed when Article 5 applies, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a proceeding or penalty about the repealed legislation still go ahead?` FALSE TRUE `it was repealed` TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 5(3) lets a proceeding about, or a penalty for, something mentioned in paragraph (2) go ahead as if the legislation had not been repealed when Article 5 applies, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
#ASSERT `Does a repeal leave this thing unrevived?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `legislation that was repealed` FALSE
#ASSERT `Does a repeal leave this thing unrevived?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `a rule of law that had been abolished` FALSE
#ASSERT `Does a repeal leave this thing unrevived?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `any other thing not in force or existing when the repeal takes effect` FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Does a repeal leave this thing unrevived?` TRUE TRUE `it was repealed` `legislation that was repealed` TRUE BECAUSE "Article 5(4) stops a repeal reviving these things when Article 5 applies and no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Does a repeal leave this thing unrevived?` FALSE TRUE `it was repealed` `legislation that was repealed` FALSE BECAUSE "Article 5(4) stops a repeal reviving these things when Article 5 applies and no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"

§§ `Articles 6 to 8`

#ASSERT `Is a reference to a repealed provision read as a reference to its replacement?` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is a reference to a repealed provision read as a reference to its replacement?` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 6 reads a reference in other Jersey legislation to a repealed and re-enacted provision as a reference to the re-enacted one when no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say how any other reference is read"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is a reference to a repealed provision read as a reference to its replacement?` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 6 reads a reference in other Jersey legislation to a repealed and re-enacted provision as a reference to the re-enacted one when no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say how any other reference is read"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is a reference to a repealed provision read as a reference to its replacement?` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 6 reads a reference in other Jersey legislation to a repealed and re-enacted provision as a reference to the re-enacted one when no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say how any other reference is read"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is a reference to a repealed provision read as a reference to its replacement?` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 6 reads a reference in other Jersey legislation to a repealed and re-enacted provision as a reference to the re-enacted one when no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say how any other reference is read"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is a reference to a repealed provision read as a reference to its replacement?` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 6 reads a reference in other Jersey legislation to a repealed and re-enacted provision as a reference to the re-enacted one when no provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say how any other reference is read"
#ASSERT `Can amended subordinate legislation still be amended or repealed by other subordinate legislation?` `an Order` `a Law`
#ASSERT `Can amended subordinate legislation still be amended or repealed by other subordinate legislation?` `an Order` `Regulations`
#ASSERT `Can amended subordinate legislation still be amended or repealed by other subordinate legislation?` `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey` `Triennial Regulations`
#ASSERT `Can amended subordinate legislation still be amended or repealed by other subordinate legislation?` `Regulations` `a Law`
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can amended subordinate legislation still be amended or repealed by other subordinate legislation?` `Regulations` `Regulations` BECAUSE "Article 7 says nothing of an amendment by Regulations of subordinate legislation made by the States"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can amended subordinate legislation still be amended or repealed by other subordinate legislation?` `an Order` `an Order` BECAUSE "Article 7 says nothing of an amendment by anything but a Law, or, for subordinate legislation not made by the States, Regulations"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can amended subordinate legislation still be amended or repealed by other subordinate legislation?` `a Law` `a Law` BECAUSE "Article 7 is about the amendment of Jersey subordinate legislation, and a Law is not subordinate legislation"
#ASSERT `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2022 1 10) (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 2 1) (YMD 2022 4 1)
#ASSERT `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2022 1 10) (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 4 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2022 1 10) (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 3 2) (YMD 2022 4 1) BECAUSE "Article 8 gives the States power to amend a Law consequentially on another Law whose period from lodging to making overlaps its own, and any other source of power is outside this Law"
#ASSERT `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2022 3 1) (YMD 2022 4 1) (YMD 2022 1 10) (YMD 2022 3 1)
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2022 3 2) (YMD 2022 4 1) (YMD 2022 1 10) (YMD 2022 3 1) BECAUSE "Article 8 gives the States power to amend a Law consequentially on another Law whose period from lodging to making overlaps its own, and any other source of power is outside this Law"
#ASSERT `Can the States amend this Law consequentially on the other Law?` (YMD 2022 1 10) (YMD 2022 6 1) (YMD 2022 2 1) (YMD 2022 3 1)

§§ `Articles 9 and 10`

#ASSERT `May a power to make subordinate legislation be used again, and to repeal, amend or replace what was made?` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a power to make subordinate legislation be used again, and to repeal, amend or replace what was made?` TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 9(1) gives these incidents to a power Jersey legislation confers unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a power to make subordinate legislation be used again, and to repeal, amend or replace what was made?` FALSE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 9(1) gives these incidents to a power Jersey legislation confers unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
#ASSERT `May a power to make subordinate legislation apply generally or be limited, or differ for different cases?` (YMD 2003 3 29) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `May a power to make subordinate legislation apply generally or be limited, or differ for different cases?` (YMD 2015 1 1) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a power to make subordinate legislation apply generally or be limited, or differ for different cases?` (YMD 2003 3 28) TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 9(2) is confined to legislation made after 28th March 2003, and the Law does not say what holds for legislation made on or before that day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a power to make subordinate legislation apply generally or be limited, or differ for different cases?` (YMD 2003 3 27) TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 9(2) is confined to legislation made after 28th March 2003, and the Law does not say what holds for legislation made on or before that day"
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a power to make subordinate legislation apply generally or be limited, or differ for different cases?` (YMD 2015 1 1) TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 9(2) lets a power conferred by Jersey legislation made after 28 March 2003 take these forms unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a power to make subordinate legislation apply generally or be limited, or differ for different cases?` (YMD 2015 1 1) FALSE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 9(2) lets a power conferred by Jersey legislation made after 28 March 2003 take these forms unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
#ASSERT `Is provision about this many cases within the power of Article 9(2)?` 1 (YMD 2015 1 1) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Is provision about this many cases within the power of Article 9(2)?` 5 (YMD 2015 1 1) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is provision about this many cases within the power of Article 9(2)?` 0 (YMD 2015 1 1) TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 9(3) speaks of one or more cases and says nothing of provision about no case"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is provision about this many cases within the power of Article 9(2)?` 1 (YMD 2015 1 1) TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 9(3) treats provision about one or more cases as within the power in Article 9(2) unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
#ASSERT `May a repeal be brought into force in part?` (YMD 2015 1 1) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `May a repeal be brought into force in part?` (YMD 2015 1 1) TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 9(4) lets a repeal made under a power Jersey legislation confers be brought into force in part unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
-- An Order of a Minister cannot use the incidental power to amend a Law; it can amend another Order.
#ASSERT NOT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `an Order` (`Legislation to be amended` OF `a Law`, FALSE, FALSE) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `an Order` (`Legislation to be amended` OF `an Order`, FALSE, FALSE) TRUE FALSE
-- Regulations may amend another Law, but not the Human Rights (Jersey) Law 2000 nor the Law giving the power.
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `Regulations` (`Legislation to be amended` OF `a Law`, FALSE, FALSE) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `Regulations` (`Legislation to be amended` OF `a Law`, TRUE, FALSE) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `Regulations` (`Legislation to be amended` OF `a Law`, FALSE, TRUE) TRUE FALSE
-- Provision that is not an amendment is not limited by (6) on the default reading.
#ASSERT `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `an Order` (`Legislation to be amended` OF `a Law`, FALSE, FALSE) FALSE FALSE
-- Where provision is made to the contrary the incidental power is displaced and the Law does not say more.
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can this instrument use the incidental power of Article 9(5) to make this provision?` `an Order` (`Legislation to be amended` OF `an Order`, FALSE, FALSE) TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 9(5) gives the incidental power unless provision is made to the contrary, and the Law does not say what the contrary provision does instead"
#ASSERT `Is this subordinate legislation treated as made under this power?` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is this subordinate legislation treated as made under this power?` TRUE FALSE BECAUSE "Article 9(7) treats subordinate legislation as made under a power when it says it is made under a power conferred by legislation and may be made under it, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Is this subordinate legislation treated as made under this power?` FALSE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 9(7) treats subordinate legislation as made under a power when it says it is made under a power conferred by legislation and may be made under it, and the Law does not say what holds in any other case"
#ASSERT `Can this technical document be incorporated by reference?` TRUE (`Facts about a document` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Can this technical document be incorporated by reference?` TRUE (`Facts about a document` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Can this technical document be incorporated by reference?` TRUE (`Facts about a document` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Can this technical document be incorporated by reference?` TRUE (`Facts about a document` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `Can this technical document be incorporated by reference?` TRUE (`Facts about a document` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `Can this technical document be incorporated by reference?` FALSE (`Facts about a document` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) BECAUSE "Article 10 gives the States power to amend a Law to allow incorporation by reference and does not itself allow it, and no such amendment is given"

§§ `Article 11`

#ASSERT `Does Article 11 apply to this instrument?` `an Order` FALSE
#ASSERT `Does Article 11 apply to this instrument?` `another instrument having legislative effect in Jersey` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Does Article 11 apply to this instrument?` `an Order` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Does Article 11 apply to this instrument?` `Regulations` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Does Article 11 apply to this instrument?` `Triennial Regulations` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Does Article 11 apply to this instrument?` `an Act of the States that is Jersey legislation` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Does Article 11 apply to this instrument?` `a Law` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Does Article 11 apply to this instrument?` `UK extended legislation` FALSE
#ASSERT `Has the duty to lay this instrument before the States been met?` `an Order` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Has the duty to lay this instrument before the States been met?` `an Order` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Has the duty to lay this instrument before the States been met?` `Regulations` FALSE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 11 does not apply to the instrument, so it does not say that the instrument must be laid"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Has the duty to lay this instrument before the States been met?` `an Order` TRUE TRUE BECAUSE "Article 11 does not apply to the instrument, so it does not say that the instrument must be laid"
-- Made after the Law: 3 sittings after laying; the third sitting is within, the fourth is not.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2022 6 1) TRUE 3 0 FALSE
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2022 6 1) TRUE 1 0 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2022 6 1) TRUE 4 0 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2022 6 1) FALSE 3 0 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2022 6 1) TRUE 3 0 TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `Regulations` FALSE (YMD 2022 6 1) TRUE 3 0 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` TRUE (YMD 2022 6 1) TRUE 3 0 FALSE
-- Made before the Law came into force: 3 sittings after 28 September 2021 on the default reading of Article 11(4).
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2021 9 27) TRUE 5 3 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2021 9 27) TRUE 1 4 FALSE
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2020 1 1) TRUE 1 3 FALSE
-- Made on the day the Law came into force: measured from laying on the default reading of the time of day.
#ASSERT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2021 9 28) TRUE 3 9 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Has this subordinate legislation ceased to have effect because the States annulled it?` `an Order` FALSE (YMD 2021 9 28) TRUE 4 0 FALSE
#ASSERT `Does annulment leave alone what was done under the instrument and the power to make further legislation?` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `Does annulment leave alone what was done under the instrument and the power to make further legislation?` FALSE BECAUSE "Article 11(2)(b) speaks of an annulment, and the instrument has not been annulled"
